  {
    "file_offset": "0x3828",
    "va": "0x10007828",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "and you will save a lot of fuel!HDrive at a steady speed,"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x389e",
    "va": "0x1000789e",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "avoiding unnecessary acceleration and braking.eKeep the same acceleration when going uphill,"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x395a",
    "va": "0x1000795a",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "and release the accelerator completely going downhill.GCongratulations!"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x39ec",
    "va": "0x100079ec",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "Your accelerating and driving speeds are very steady.JChange up gears sooner."
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x3a8a",
    "va": "0x10007a8a",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "The gear change indicator can help you with this.SDo not stay in 1st or 2nd gear too long,"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x3b42",
    "va": "0x10007b42",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "use the higher gears as soon as possible."
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x3b96",
    "va": "0x10007b96",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "In town,you can use 5th gear as soon as you are at a constant speed.If you have a 6-speed gearbox, change to 6th gear from 40 mph.QSometimes gear changes like"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x3cd6",
    "va": "0x10007cd6",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "3rd to 5th or 4th to 2nd can be more fuel efficient.7Congratulations!"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x3d64",
    "va": "0x10007d64",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "Your gear changing is very efficient!~Take your foot off the accelerator,you will be driving for free as the engine will cut off fuel injection when engine braking.mAnticipate other vehicles' movements:"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x3efc",
    "va": "0x10007efc",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "ease off the accelerator as soon as you notice there is traffic ahead.|Red light in 300 yards:ease off the accelerator to allow time for it to change to green and for the other cars to pull away."
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x4088",
    "va": "0x10008088",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "UGreen light in 300 yards:"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x40c0",
    "va": "0x100080c0",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "ease off the accelerator to anticipate it changing to red.ECongratulations!"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x415a",
    "va": "0x1000815a",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "You are taking full advantage of your cars inertia.qDo not leave the engine idling, even in winter:it is more efficient to drive off as soon as you start the engine.`Check the tyre pressures every 3 months,"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x42fa",
    "va": "0x100082fa",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "preferably keeping them at the eco or motorway levels.iRemove the roof rack and roof box when not in use:"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x43d0",
    "va": "0x100083d0",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "they slow down the car and increase fuel consumption.ZDo not leave unnecessary objects in the vehicle:"
  },
  {
    "file_offset": "0x44a0",
    "va": "0x100084a0",
    "encoding": "utf16le",
    "text": "extra weight increases fuel consumption.PIn summer, use the air conditioning on motorways,"
